repository-code: "https://github.com/Finance-broski/graveyard"
url: "https://finance-broski.github.io/graveyard.html"
abstract: >-
  A forward-running public record of killed quantitative-research hypotheses on Indian and
  global markets. Each entry states the hypothesis, the preregistered bar it had to clear, the
  verdict with measured numbers, the number of configurations run, and a cause-of-death class:
  no-signal, infra-invalid, cost-wall, regime, handed-back, structural-wall, capital-gated,
  parked or resurrected. The ledger exists to publish the denominator that most research
  reporting omits, and includes five public retractions of the author's own prior claims.
  Rows too close to live book construction are withheld and counted rather than removed.
keywords:
  - negative results
  - research transparency
  - preregistration
  - backtest overfitting
  - survivorship bias
  - quantitative finance
  - replication
